ggml-cpu: quantize a strided src1 of the repack matmul row by row
Fold-into: upstream/ggml-cpu

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

Finding F-REPACK-1 of fuzz-ops, task #173. The repack MUL_MAT of ggml-cpu
(Q4_0 and Q8_0 weights in the repack buffer) quantizes src1 in groups of 4
rows with ggml_quantize_mat_t, which reads the 4 rows at a stride of ne10
floats. When src1 is a view with nb11 != ne10 * 4 (for example a view of a
wider tensor), the group reads the wrong values, and the product is wrong:
on the phone the error was up to 4.7e9 times the strict bound of the case.

This patch copies each group of 4 rows into a contiguous buffer first when
the rows of src1 are strided. A contiguous src1 takes the same path as
before.

Evidence (2026-09-23):
- The op fuzzer on the host (x86, the release and debug none builds): the
  12 above-loose findings of the Q4_0 repack matmul kinds pass with this
  patch. The test suite: release 0 findings; debug only the value asserts of
  task #128.
- The phone check (OnePlus 13, thermal status 0, battery 28 C, not on a
  charger): the first 600 cases of the op pack (sha256 d0474fad) with the
  libraries of the current series against the same tree with this patch.
  Only libggml-cpu.so differs between the two sets. On the CPU, 587 runs are
  bit-identical. The other 13 are Q4_0 repack MUL_MATs with a strided f32
  src1 of 4 to 212 rows: before this patch each was above the loose bound
  (ratio 3.3e3 to 4.7e9), with it each is within the loose bound (5 pass, 8
  above the strict bound only, as the contiguous Q4_0 cases). The CPU
  verdicts of the 600 cases: above-loose 13 before, 0 after.

Measurement: llama-bench on the phone CPU (6 threads, -fa 1, 5 repetitions,
one warmup run, the order before, after, before, after):
  tg32, 4B Q8_0:   before 11.32 +- 0.04 and 11.23 +- 0.15, after
                   11.40 +- 0.18 and 11.31 +- 0.06 tokens/s
  pp128, 2B Q8_0:  before 236.81 +- 0.77 and 235.48 +- 0.68, after
                   233.70 +- 1.84 and 235.86 +- 1.47 tokens/s
No difference is above the spread. A contiguous src1 adds one compare for
each group of 4 rows.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp
index f5e419c..31e7581 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <cstring>
 #include <cassert>
 #include <cstdio>  // for GGML_ASSERT
+#include <vector>
 
 #include "repack.h"
 
@@ -4290,6 +4291,13 @@ template <typename BLOC_TYPE, int64_t INTER_SIZE, int64_t NB_COLS, ggml_type PAR
 
         const ggml_from_float_t from_float = ggml_get_type_traits_cpu(PARAM_TYPE)->from_float;
 
+        // ggml_quantize_mat_t reads 4 rows at a stride of ne10 floats. When the rows of src1 have a
+        // different stride (for example a view of a wider tensor), each group of 4 rows goes into a
+        // contiguous buffer first. The buffer has 4*ne10 floats and exists only for such a src1.
+        GGML_ASSERT(nb10 == sizeof(float));
+        const bool         rows_contiguous = nb11 == (size_t) ne10 * sizeof(float);
+        std::vector<float> rows4(rows_contiguous ? 0 : (size_t) 4 * ne10);
+
         // INFO: Quantization is done in planes to avoid extra complexity in chunking.
         // Flattening dimensions not multiple of INTER_SIZE would require extra handling depending on how
         // the planes are broadcast.
@@ -4298,8 +4306,14 @@ template <typename BLOC_TYPE, int64_t INTER_SIZE, int64_t NB_COLS, ggml_type PAR
             char * wdata_ptr = wdata + i12 * nbw2;
 
             for (int64_t i11 = ith * 4; i11 < ne11 - ne11 % 4; i11 += nth * 4) {
-                ggml_quantize_mat_t<INTER_SIZE, PARAM_TYPE>((float *) (data_ptr + i11 * nb11),
-                                                            (void *) (wdata_ptr + i11 * nbw1), 4, ne10);
+                float * rows = (float *) (data_ptr + i11 * nb11);
+                if (!rows_contiguous) {
+                    for (int64_t r = 0; r < 4; r++) {
+                        memcpy(rows4.data() + r * ne10, data_ptr + (i11 + r) * nb11, ne10 * sizeof(float));
+                    }
+                    rows = rows4.data();
+                }
+                ggml_quantize_mat_t<INTER_SIZE, PARAM_TYPE>(rows, (void *) (wdata_ptr + i11 * nbw1), 4, ne10);
             }
 
             const int64_t i11_processed = ne11 - ne11 % 4;
